 "reading": "Every option handler in this engine is a plain assignment (plus a cache clear), so the FINAL state cannot depend on the order two assignments were made: setting A then B leaves the same pair of values as B then A. Order-independence is therefore expected by construction here and is a weak result on its own. What the report calls `UseNNUE > NNUEArch > NnueFile` precedence is GATING, not ordering: NnueFile has no effect while UseNNUE is false. That is what the no-effect sweep can see, and it is the sweep that carries the weight of this section.",
 "caveat": "A fixed-depth probe cannot see an option that only matters outside the positions searched. NO_EFFECT here means 'no effect on this probe', which is a weaker claim than 'no effect' and is the same limit that makes bench blind to a switch.",
